  <h1>Nylon 3D printing processes</h1>
  <div class="quick-answer">
    <p class="qa-label">Quick answer</p>
    <p>Nylon is printed four main ways: <strong>SLS</strong> and <strong>MJF</strong> (and Stratasys's <strong>SAF</strong>), which fuse PA11/PA12 powder in a powder bed and dominate professional production; and <strong>FDM</strong>, which extrudes nylon filament and is the route most individuals and small workshops use. Powder processes give support-free, near-isotropic parts; FDM is far cheaper to access but is anisotropic and moisture-sensitive.</p>
  </div>

